@startuml wt_signing_broadcast_failover
title WT failover around signing and broadcast
hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 75
participant "Niso i" as N
participant "Boomlet i" as B
participant "Iso i" as I
participant "Other four peers" as P
participant "Candidate WT" as C
participant "Bitcoin network" as Chain

alt A complete signed transaction is already retained
  N -> N: Verify full transaction, descriptor and approved tx_id
  N -> Chain: Broadcast or rebroadcast the exact transaction
else Coordination is needed for signing or fragment collection
  N -> B: Propose WT failover
  opt A MuSig2 secret nonce is live
    alt Exact signing session can finish
      B -> I: Continue identical message, keys, tweaks and nonce context
      I -> B: Local signing contribution
      B -> B: Complete once, consume nonce and retain immutable fragment
    else Session requires abort
      B -> B: Erase unused nonce and record aborted session
      B -> I: Coordinate erasure of unused session nonce
      I -> I: Erase unused nonce; retain completed signing output
    end
  end

  ref over B,C
    02_common_switch.puml
    Review, freeze and certify the candidate after live nonce resolution.
    A signing or exported withdrawal retains its initialized status.
  end ref

  alt Final ABORT
    B -> B: Resume matching local phase with retained signing disposition
  else Final ACTIVATE
    alt This peer still needs a signature
      ref over B,C
        06_digging_failover.puml
        Use the obligation and recovery-ping portions\nto obtain five fresh reached pings under the installed head.
      end ref
      C -> B: Current-head reached collection
      N -> B: Hydrated PSBT for the same approved transaction
      B -> B: Verify reached evidence, descriptor, tx_id,\ntransaction semantics, sighash policy and milestones
      B -> I: Validated signing package and fresh public nonce
      I -> B: Matching local MuSig2 contribution
      B -> B: Produce signature once and retain immutable fragment
    else This peer already produced its fragment
      B -> B: Retain exact fragment and required peer-continuation state
    end
    B -> N: Retained signed fragment and Boomlet-authenticated new-head envelope
    N -> N: Persist fragment and required recovery evidence
    N -> C: Forward Boomlet-authenticated fragment envelope
    C -> C: Verify and durably retain exact fragment
    C -> B: Head-bound FragmentReceipt over origin, approved ID and digest
    B -> B: Record dissemination; retain own exact fragment
    P -> C: Four retained signed fragments through authenticated paths
    C -> C: Verify all five, descriptor, final transaction and approved tx_id
    C -> Chain: Broadcast exact approved transaction
    C -> N: Complete signed transaction and head-bound CompletionReceipt
    N -> B: Exact complete transaction and receipt
    B -> B: Verify complete transaction, all five fragments and own SAR duty
    B -> B: Mark COMPLETED_RETAINED; retain own fragment and closed IDs
    B -> B: Erase completed private delay state and consumed session secrets
    note over N,C
      An untrusted holder receipt cannot authorize fragment erasure.
      Archive erasure requires permanent setup-identity retirement.
      Consumed secret nonces are never used for another signing attempt.
    end note
  end
end
@enduml
